model n1_q
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30
  note "T, tally 2.3 (#247), C-4's clause (L §5.14, E §5 step 1; from the critic's n1_q.tally, its day a window row): a later version that changes a hole-day instance makes an adjustment whose existence is that hole, so a count or a sum over adjustments that could hold it is the hole (the plan's §9.4: its words and register hand-stored). a1, known 2026-03-20, falls inside pay's window: pinned before it the pay is changed (1), pinned on or after it it isn't (0)"

source s "s"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input amt: money PLN
input w: date
input d_at: date

move pay: transfers
  on w
  at d_at
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d_at = 2026-03-01 "s"
  w = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-25) "s"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version a0
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"

version a1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-20
  replace amt = 150.00 PLN "s"

ask adj: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04)
ask adj_sum: sum(a.change for a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04)
ask adj_p05: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) with w = 2026-03-05
ask adj_p20: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) with w = 2026-03-20
ask adj_p25: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) with w = 2026-03-25
ask adj_sum_p05: sum(a.change for a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) with w = 2026-03-05
ask b_mar: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask fl: flows(pay, 2026-03)
ask k0322: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) as known 2026-03-22
ask ex: explain bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
